msgid "@jridgewell/sourcemap-codec"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sourcemap-codec_README.md:3
msgid ""
"Encode/decode the `mappings` property of a "
"[sourcemap](https://docs.google.com/document/d"
"/1U1RGAehQwRypUTovF1KRlpiOFze0b-_2gc6fAH0KY0k/edit)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sourcemap-codec_README.md:6
msgid "Why?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sourcemap-codec_README.md:8
msgid ""
"Sourcemaps are difficult to generate and manipulate, because the "
"`mappings` property – the part that actually links the generated code "
"back to the original source – is encoded using an obscure method called "
"[Variable-length quantity](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Variable-"
"length_quantity). On top of that, each segment in the mapping contains "
"offsets rather than absolute indices, which means that you can't look at "
"a segment in isolation – you have to understand the whole sourcemap."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sourcemap-codec_README.md:10
msgid "This package makes the process slightly easier."
msgstr ""

